Here is a quick introduction to some of the features Lithic has to offer:
⁂⁂⁂
title: Introduction/1
parent: Introduction
stream-list: Introduction/1/explain Introduction/1/demo Introduction/1/code
type: text/markdown

## 1. Zero Friction Entry & Editing
⁂⁂⁂
title: Introduction/1/explain
parent: Introduction/1
type: text/markdown

Put all new items into today's journal and simply describe what you are doing. Lithic will automatically track the time between bullets.

**Double-click any node to edit it.** Press `Enter` while editing to create a new trailing node below it, or use `Shift+Enter` to add a new line within the current node. 

Use CamelCase or `[[links]]` to create stub pages and then click on them to fill them out.
⁂⁂⁂
title: Introduction/1/demo
parent: Introduction/1
type: text/markdown

#### Demonstration:
* **Double-click this node to edit it**, then press `Enter` to create a new item right below it.
* Link somewhere: [[Secret Project]]
⁂⁂⁂
title: Introduction/1/code
parent: Introduction/1
type: text/markdown

```markdown
#### Demonstration:
* **Double-click this node to edit it**, then press `Enter` to create a new item right below it.
* Link somewhere: [[Secret Project]]
```
