## 6. AutoTable
⁂⁂⁂
title: Introduction/6/explain
parent: Introduction/6
type: text/markdown

Create dynamic tables easily using the `<<AutoTable>>` macro (which takes a required number of columns and optional column headers) for quick structured data entry.
⁂⁂⁂
title: Introduction/6/demo
parent: Introduction/6
type: text/markdown

#### Demonstration:
**Double-click this node to edit it** and see how the macro looks under the hood:

<<AutoTable 3 "One Two Three">>
⁂⁂⁂
title: Introduction/6/code
parent: Introduction/6
type: text/markdown

```markdown
#### Demonstration:
**Double-click this node to edit it** and see how the macro looks under the hood:

<<AutoTable 3 "One Two Three">>
```
⁂⁂⁂
title: Introduction/7
parent: Introduction
stream-list: Introduction/7/explain Introduction/7/demo Introduction/7/code
type: text/markdown

## 7. Calc
⁂⁂⁂
title: Introduction/7/explain
parent: Introduction/7
type: text/markdown

Perform inline math evaluations directly in your notes. Ending your formula with `=` displays the full equation and answer using KaTeX. Dropping the `=` displays only the plaintext result.
⁂⁂⁂
title: Introduction/7/demo
parent: Introduction/7
type: text/markdown

#### Demonstration:
**Double-click this node to edit it** and try adding or removing the `=` at the end of the macros to see the difference!

Full KaTeX equation: <<calc "5 + 10 * 2=">>
Plaintext answer only: <<calc "5 + 10 * 2">>
⁂⁂⁂
title: Introduction/7/code
parent: Introduction/7
type: text/markdown

```markdown
#### Demonstration:
**Double-click this node to edit it** and try adding or removing the `=` at the end of the macros to see the difference!

Full KaTeX equation: <<calc "5 + 10 * 2=">>
Plaintext answer only: <<calc "5 + 10 * 2">>
```
⁂⁂⁂
title: Introduction/8
parent: Introduction
stream-list: Introduction/8/explain Introduction/8/demo Introduction/8/code
